  "title": "Experiential blindness: sensation without sight",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "57a73575-1893-447b-89b8-f37a654f06ed",
      "text": "Experiential blindness is blindness despite something like normal visual sensation, from a lack of sensorimotor understanding. Noë finds it in adults whose congenital cataracts were removed and in people wearing inverting lenses, and takes it as evidence for the enactive approach.",
